  m_Name: COC2_L4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::LessonData
  lessonID: 8
  cocID: COC_02
  lessonTitle: OHS Policies and PPE
  description: Learn the occupational safety procedures and personal protective equipment
    (PPE) used to stay safe while working on network installations.
  lessonSceneName: LessonScene
  requiredGoldLessonID: 7
  learningObjectives:
  - "• Identify OHS policies and procedures."
  - "• Use appropriate personal protective equipment."
  subtopics:
  - subtopicID: 0801
    subtopicName: "OHS Policies"
  - subtopicID: 0802
    subtopicName: PPE
  slides:
  - subtopicID: 0801
    slideType: 0
    content: "The following are the Occupational Safety and Health Procedures while working that aim to protect the health, safety and welfare of all people in the workplace.\n\n1. Do not work alone so that there is someone who can take care of you in case of emergency.\n\n2. Always power off the computer and unplug the computer before and after working on it.\n\n3. Remove all liquids from the work area to avoid getting electrocuted or accidentally damaging computer parts."
    image: {fileID: 0}
  - subtopicID: 0801
    slideType: 0
    content: "4. Be careful with tools that may cause a short circuit.\n\n5. Always ground or discharge yourself before touching any part of the computer.\n\n6. Do not use excessive force if components do not fit into place.\n\n7. Clean the area before and after using it to maintain sanitation and prevent accidents."
    image: {fileID: 0}
  - subtopicID: 0801
    slideType: 0
    content: "8. Hold the components on the edges and do not touch the Integrated Circuits (IC) parts.\n\n9. Always wear personal protective equipment (PPE) in accordance with the organization’s OHS procedures and practices.\n\n10. Make sure that the pins are properly aligned when connecting a cable connector.\n\n11. Follow established contingency procedures during workplace accidents, fires, and other emergencies.\n\n12. Use a brush, compressed air, or a blower to clean the computer system."
    image: {fileID: 0}
  - subtopicID: 0802
    slideType: 0
    content: "<size=115%><b>Personal Protective Equipment</b></size>\n\nIt refers to protective clothing, helmets, goggles, or other gear designed to protect the wearer’s body or clothing from injury by electrical hazard, heat, chemicals and infection, for job-related occupational safety and health purposes.\n\n<b>Goggles</b> — A large spectacle, with shields around the rims, for protecting the eyes from dust, excessive light, wind etc.\n\n<b>Rubber sole</b> — A special type of shoes used to prevent electrical shock and for waterproofing and insulating purposes."
    image: {fileID: 0}
  - subtopicID: 0802
    slideType: 0
    content: "<b>Apron</b> — A garment worn over the front of the body as a protection for one’s cloth\n\n<b>Face mask</b> — A covering for the face to prevent the inhaling or absorbing dust and other chemicals.\n\n<b>Gloves</b> — The covering material with a separate sheath for each finger used for hand protection.\n\n<b>Anti-static wrist strap</b> — Use to prevent body from building up static-electricity that usually damage electronics or cause safety issues."
    image: {fileID: 0}
